"A transparent wash lets the paper show through.": "1f7120240537",
"Chinese ink painting uses black ink, made mostly of soot and glue, and water. With one black, the painter makes many grays by changing how much water is in the brush. Chinese painters speak of ink having five colors, meaning its many tones, from dark to pale and from dry to wet.": "c98e333882ee",
"Each stroke of ink is final.": "a2b6a6bc6f64",
"Give three painters the same apple. One uses watercolor, one uses oil paint, and one uses Chinese ink. Their pictures will look different, but the bigger difference is in how they work: what they paint first, what they paint last, and what they can change.": "546f0793bfe8",
"Give three painters the same apple. One uses watercolor, one uses oil paint, and one uses Chinese ink. Their pictures will look different, but the bigger difference is in how they work: what they paint first, what they paint last, and what they can change. Watercolor is semi-transparent. Each layer lets the layers and the paper beneath it show through. So the white of the paper becomes the light in the picture, and white areas are often simply left unpainted. A pale color comes from adding more water, not white paint. Many watercolor painters work from light to dark, laying one thin wash over another. Oil paint covers well and dries slowly. A thin layer may be dry to the touch in a few days, and a thick one takes longer. Because it stays wet, the painter can blend colors and make changes. One traditional way is to work from the darkest colors to the lightest, and a light color can be painted right over a dark one. Chinese ink painting uses black ink, made mostly of soot and glue, and water. With one black, the painter makes many grays by changing how much water is in the brush. Chinese painters speak of ink having five colors, meaning its many tones, from dark to pale and from dry to wet. Ink painting is usually done on xuan paper, which is very absorbent. Raw xuan paper drinks in water so quickly that ink spreads and blurs. Once a stroke is painted, it cannot be changed or erased. That is why ink painting asks for so much planning and practice before the brush touches the paper. None of these is better than the others. Each one invites a different way of thinking. A watercolor painter plans where to keep the white, an oil painter can build up and change the picture over many days, and an ink painter decides each stroke before making it. Try all three, and see which way of thinking suits you.": "1d9dc4c552a6",
"Gouache is opaque, so it hides what is under it.": "e7d5cc4b8ac1",
"How does an ink painter make light and dark grays with only black ink?": "b7f86cfae3b7",
"In watercolor, where does the white in a picture usually come from?": "d8f5532844ca",
"Ink painting is usually done on xuan paper, which is very absorbent. Raw xuan paper drinks in water so quickly that ink spreads and blurs. Once a stroke is painted, it cannot be changed or erased. That is why ink painting asks for so much planning and practice before the brush touches the paper.": "683fe31e9032",
"None of these is better than the others. Each one invites a different way of thinking. A watercolor painter plans where to keep the white, an oil painter can build up and change the picture over many days, and an ink painter decides each stroke before making it. Try all three, and see which way of thinking suits you.": "9425ae67f605",
"Oil paint covers well and dries slowly. A thin layer may be dry to the touch in a few days, and a thick one takes longer. Because it stays wet, the painter can blend colors and make changes. One traditional way is to work from the darkest colors to the lightest, and a light color can be painted right over a dark one.": "aa977e09b5d2",
"Oil painters build up the picture layer by layer.": "c12b0e6936f3",
